					<p class="body1" align="left"><span class="body1 style73"> <h2>News archive</h2><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-12-18 | Monday</font></strong><br><br>first day back on the real job, and, thanks to one helluva wind-storm,&nbsp;it didn&#39;t take any time at all to get back into the routine of &quot;clean-up&nbsp;man.&quot;&nbsp; it feels good to be home, but&nbsp;this odd sense of longing for that thick LA smog sure&nbsp;is tuggin&#39; at the heart strings.&nbsp; big up&#39;s to all the folks who came out to el rey on friday for the finale - i couldn&#39;t have asked for a better conclusion to a great tour.&nbsp; and many thanks to all the well-wishers at home who kept us in their thoughts and prayers; we made it back to spread love to those battered and bruised by nature.&nbsp; lemme know what you need - i got that...<br /><br />on the strength...<br /><br />RA<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-12-17 | Sunday</font></strong><br><br>sunday. whoo.<br />
<br />
the next couple weeks are going to be busy for the MassLine camp.&nbsp; the
Lovework Album Release party is getting put together, RA and i have
just returned from the tour, the Blue Scholars are getting the
recording of the new record finished, and we&#39;re all gearing up to rock
it with Big World Breaks for the New Year show at Neumo&#39;s.<br />
<br />
the storm has cleared and the power is slowly returning to the homes in
and around Seattle.&nbsp; tonight would be a good time to just relax.<br />
<br />
sit back on the couch with somebody you care about, turn on the TV,
grab a glass of San Pelligrino, a %&amp;*$ in a box and let the good
times roll.<br />
<br />
<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-12-14 | Thursday</font></strong><br><br><img src="http://www.obeseproductions.com/image/flyers/dopeWEB.jpg" alt="Dope Emporium" title="Dope Emporium" width="342" height="477" align="absmiddle" /><br /><br />Massline representing in three places at once tonight: <strong>Common Market</strong> at the <em>Canes Bar &amp; Grill</em> in the <strong>619</strong> (21+, $15 8PM), and for those in the 206, one last reminder to brave the rain to hit up <strong>Dope Emporium </strong>(All-ages, FREE 7PM) at the <a href="http://www.capitolhillarts.com/" target="_blank" title="CHAC">Capitol Hill Arts Center</a> where Abyssinian Creole and Geologic will be among those in the massive lineup, along with our favorite party rockin <strong>DJ daps1</strong>. Ab Creole&#39;s doing double duty, also rockin the <strong>Andre Nickatina</strong> show down the street at <strong>Neumo&#39;s</strong> (All-ages, $15 9PM).<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-12-13 | Wednesday</font></strong><br><br>what a difference a day (off) makes.&nbsp; the rest and relaxation made for a much more enthusiastic performance, and i sincerely hope, for the sake of two fans who drove five and-a-half hours to see CM rock in lieu of the massline show in tempe, that the love was adequately conveyed through the music.&nbsp; aint no glitz and glam about ABQ, sun - this place is full of real-ass folks workin&#39; two jobs to pay bills, so you already KNOW i aint trippin&#39; about low attendance; y&#39;all keep doin&#39; ya thing out here.<br /><br />in all things...<br /><br />peace.<br /><br />RA<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-12-12 | Tuesday</font></strong><br><br>Finals week. Feeling like a student myself again, cramming for the studio sessions in the coming weeks. Somehow, we&#39;ll also find time this month to rehearse with the homies <strong>Big World Breaks</strong> for our end of the year shows at Neumo&#39;s. Oh, you haven&#39;t heard yet? Well, the entire Massline fam - Blue Scholars, Common Market and Gabriel Teodros - is performing alongside the illest live hip-hop band in the Northwest: Big World Breaks for <strong>TWO SHOWS</strong> at <strong>Neumo&#39;s</strong> (in Seattle) to close out 2006. We&#39;ve done several shows together around town, but this will be the first time we&#39;ll all be onstage at the SAME TIME. <br /><br />And, tickets are on sale NOW: <a href="http://ticketswest.rdln.com/Artist.aspx?evt=51855">www.ticketswest.com</a>.<br /><br />Ah, I can hear the grumbling already: well, if the music will be played by a live band, then where&#39;s <strong>Sabzi</strong> gonna be??? Don&#39;t fret, ladies. He&#39;ll be hypemanning it up for us. Sike. He&#39;ll be onstage and busy, we promise. Maybe even pull out the new toy he pulled out at the last Common Market and Blue Scholars shows in the town (if you were there, you know what we&#39;re talking about - shhh!).<br /> <br />If you&#39;re plugged into the myspace matrix, then take a detour to the <a href="http://profile.myspace.com/index.cfm?fuseaction=user.viewprofile&amp;friendid=33002630">Big World Breaks myspace page</a> and download some of their live cuts. I&#39;m pumped to hear how it&#39;ll all come together.  But if you&#39;ve ever seen em live before, you know it&#39;s always heat. One last thing - the <strong>Dec. 30 show is all-ages</strong> and the <strong>Dec. 31 show is 21+</strong>. <a href="http://www.masslinemedia.com/calendar.php">Check the calendar for more info</a>.<br /><br />geo<br /> <p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><center><div class="pagenumbers"><A HREF="archive.php?from=250">[&lt;&lt;]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=0">[1]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=5">[2]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=10">[3]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=15">[4]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=20">[5]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=25">[6]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=30">[7]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=35">[8]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=40">[9]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=45">[10]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=50">[11]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=55">[12]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=60">[13]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=65">[14]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=70">[15]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=75">[16]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=80">[17]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=85">[18]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=90">[19]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=95">[20]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=100">[21]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=105">[22]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=110">[23]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=115">[24]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=120">[25]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=125">[26]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=130">[27]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=135">[28]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=140">[29]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=145">[30]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=150">[31]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=155">[32]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=160">[33]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=165">[34]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=170">[35]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=175">[36]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=180">[37]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=185">[38]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=190">[39]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=195">[40]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=200">[41]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=205">[42]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=210">[43]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=215">[44]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=220">[45]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=225">[46]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=230">[47]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=235">[48]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=240">[49]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=245">[50]</A> <A HREF